AI Usage Log Entry 2
Task ID/Title: Git and PowerShell Setup and Troubleshooting
Purpose of AI Use:
Debugging and development environment setup. AI was used to fix errors while cloning the repository,
running the dev server and pushing my branch.

Prompt: "git clone gives 'fatal: could not create work tree dir: Permission denied' in PowerShell." / "My
changes show in VS Code but the browser still runs the old code." / "git push says 'Everything
up-to-date' but my new files aren't on GitHub."
AI Response: The AI explained that the terminal was opened in C:\Windows\system32 (a protected
folder) and to clone into a folder in my user directory instead. It suggested checking the file on disk with
Select-String to confirm unsaved changes, and explained that git push only sends commits, so the
changes had to be staged and committed first. It also explained renaming the branch and setting the
upstream on the first push.
AI-Suggested Content:
cd ~ ; mkdir Projects ; cd Projects ; git clone <repo-url>
Select-String -Path src\pages\LoginPage.tsx -Pattern "Logging in"
git branch -m feature/login-ui
git push -u origin feature/login-ui
git status, then git add / git commit before git push
Validation:
Each command was run in PowerShell and the result was checked (repo cloned, file contents
confirmed on disk, branch visible on GitHub with the expected commits).
Decision:
Accepted. The commands solved each issue.
Reflection:
I learned the difference between saving a file, committing it and pushing it, and why the first push needs
-u origin <branch> so it does not push to the branch I started from.
Responsible Person:
Dany Abou Saleh



