AI Usage Log Entry 4
Task ID/Title:
Add AuthContext, Protected Route and Logout
Purpose of AI Use:
Code generation. AI was used to implement shared authentication state so the login page,
ProtectedRoute and Navbar all use one source of truth for the logged-in user.

Prompt: "Now let's do AuthContext so ProtectedRoute and the navbar know who is logged in, and add
logout."
AI Response: The AI generated an AuthProvider (stores the token and user, persists them in
localStorage so a refresh keeps the session), a useAuth hook, and updates to App.tsx, ProtectedRoute
and Navbar (email, Dashboard and Logout when logged in). It split the context into separate files to
satisfy the project's ESLint react-refresh rule.
AI-Suggested Content:
• src/context/AuthContext.tsx, authState.ts and useAuth.ts.
• App wrapped in AuthProvider; ProtectedRoute and Navbar read useAuth().
• LoginPage calls login(token, user) instead of writing to localStorage directly.
Validation:
Tested in the browser: /dashboard redirects to /login when logged out, login shows my email and
Logout in the navbar, refreshing keeps me logged in, and Logout returns to /login and locks the
dashboard. npm run build passed.
Decision:
Modified before use. Comments were rewritten without metaphors. I informed Krish because the
change touches his Navbar, ProtectedRoute and App files.
Reflection:
I now understand why a Context is better than every component reading localStorage on its own: logout
and future changes to token storage happen in one place. Storing the token in localStorage is a
decision the team should still review for security.
Responsible Person:
Dany Abou Saleh
